    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Perform CPR on a firm flat surface. Apply manual left uterine displacement (LUD) to relieve aortocaval compress - do ⍉tilt the pt or table (↓CPR effectiveness). The gravid uterus compresses the IVC & aorta in the supine position, potentially reducing venous return by up to 25%."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": {
      "rule": "auto",
      "value": 1
     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "2025 Update: Initiate resuscitative hysterotomy (perimortem cesarean delivery) STAT upon recognition of ♡ arrest when the uterus = @ or above the umbilicus (-20 wks gestation). The goal = delivery w/in 5 min. Do ⍉wait 4-5 min b4 initiating preparation - begin STAT. Consider ECPR (extracorporeal CPR) if strd resuscitation fails."
     }
    ]
   },
